      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is entirely possible with stop action animators on avatars currently. It is difficult to set up however, but if you are looking for something similar to this I have an avatar with a functional drum kit using this method.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-07-27T15:32:15.884Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I would love for there to be a built-in feature that allows players to pull out an instrument on their left or right hand, select a song from a list and then start playing it in-game for other players to hear.\n\nUsers could import their own MIDI files to a folder somewhere in the game files and then select from a list in-game to play them.\n\n\"Player instrument\" volume could be adjusted in the settings, and \"Instruments\" could be toggled on/off in the safety settings.\n\nAdditionally, if this works then in the future a sync feature could allow players could form ensembles to play songs together.\n\nThe instruments could be stylized for VRChat and emit little music notes when being played.\n\nThis idea is inspired by MIDI instruments in games like Starbound and Maple Story 2.",
